  "name": "S1 control benchmark - positives and the decoys that look like them",
  "description": "The panel the classifier is measured on. **Positives**: one or two human members of every census family, chosen to include the known-hard cases - CACNA1G's EEDD filter and its complete absence of any Cav-specific domain, TRPC3 and TRPM8 with no PF00520 at all, TRPV6 against TRPV1 (identical architecture, hundredfold difference in P_Ca/P_Na), GRIA2 whose permeability is set after transcription. **Decoys**: every family catalogued so it can be excluded - SCN5A (the same architecture as CACNA1C), CACNB1 and CACNG2 (calcium-channel symbols, one of them an AMPA receptor subunit), KCNMA1 and ANO1 (Ca2+-activated, conducting K+ and Cl-), TRPM4 (inside the TRPM family and Ca2+-impermeable), ATP2A1 and SLC8A1 (calcium transport, no pore), CALM1 and CASR (calcium binding and sensing, no pore), STIM1 and MICU1 (inside census complexes and not pores). Every decoy is a hazard with a number, and a decoy that classifies as a calcium channel is a failed test, not a surprise.",
